From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:04:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scene: nodes keep where they've been through World3D.shift()

A floating origin moves a world and every node in it at once
(World3D::shift()). Some nodes keep global positions outside their
transforms, which the shift left behind: a Trail3D's points (it was
drawn stretched back to where it had been), GPUParticles3D's last
position (its emitter speed was the whole shift for a frame), the
places Camera3D, AudioListener3D and AudioStreamPlayer3D track for
the Doppler effect (the same, in pitch), and a joint holding a body to
the world (the world end stayed behind and pulled the body back where
the physics engine couldn't shift its space).

Node3D::world_shifted() is called by whatever shifted the world on the
nodes that moved with it, and these move what they keep, or make the
joint again where it now is. A one-body joint that didn't move with the
world is made again too (Joint3D::update_server_transform()), as a
physics engine that shifts its whole space moved its world end.

No upstream issue yet.

Test: after a shift of the world, a Trail3D's length and a Camera3D's
tracked Doppler speed are what they were, and a body hanging from a
joint with no second body stays where it hangs, inside the shifted
world or outside it (Purr's samples/world).
